# FRAMEWORK-IMPROVEMENTS.md — {{product-name}}

> **How to use:** instantiated in F0, together with `STATE.md`
> (`Maestro/workflows/W00-project-kickoff.md`), and maintained **since day 0**: whenever the
> work reveals a new pitfall, a pattern with a measured gain, a framework friction point or a
> reusable block, the agent who lived it records it here **in the moment** — never "at the end
> of the project" (late retrospectives only recover what the commits tell; the rest is lost).
> Consolidated at the close of F6/F7/F8 and, in F9, at the profile's cadence
> (`Maestro/agents/13-guardians/README.md` §Cadences per profile); sent to the upstream framework
> via `Maestro/playbooks/report-framework-improvements.md`. Lives at the **project root**.

> **Sanitization (mandatory):** this file leaves the project. No entry contains personal
> data, customer names, secrets or confidential domain detail — the lesson is written in
> general form; the evidence points to paths/commits, without pasting sensitive content.

---

*Format of each entry (same across the five sections): **what → why → evidence → suggested
destination in the framework**. An entry without a why and without evidence is not sent — it
is opinion, not lesson (`Maestro/knowledge/README.md` §Golden rule). Always distinguish
**new** (this project discovered it) from **cross-validated** (the framework already said it;
this project confirmed it in another domain — the confirmation is also reported, because it
raises the pattern's confidence).*

